    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58819" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κομμ-ωτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for embellishment</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσκησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Am.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποικιλία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					24.303c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνι διαφέρει τοῦ κ. τὸ κοσμητικὸν τῆς
					ἰατρικῆς μέρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					12.434
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>UP</u>
				1.9
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) the <i>art of
			embellishment</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				463b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.183
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>: metaph., of style, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόσμος τις ἐπικείμενος ἔξωθεν κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Id.</u>
					1.12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				24.303c
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς,
			ἔχειν</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				1064
			</span></i>.</div>
